  Oliver Seiler writes:
  I'm sorry, but what is PPL?

Privately Produced Law.  Tom Morrow's article "Privately Produced Law", 
found in Extropy #7 is a good overview of the subject.  In brief, since
competition increases quality and lowers cost, the idea is to have a 
market in everything governments usually monopolize.  Read _The Machinery
of Freedom: Guide to a Radical Capitalism_ by David Friedman, and then
read _The Enterprise of Law_ by Bruce Benson.

In Laissez Faire's November catalog there's a book on the law of saga
Iceland, called _Bloodtaking and Peacemaking_ by William Ian Miller.
Has anyone read it?  I started picking up Icelandic sagas after reading
Machinery, and when I eventually read them I'd prefer to do it in order.
Does anyone have a complete chronological list of the sagas?  

