Having just finished _The Illuminati Papers_, I have been thinking a
lot about the issue of drugs.  RAW seems to think highly of their use
in Self Transformation.  I have tried none at all (well, one and a
half beers at one high school party and one-half cup of straight vodka
once in college, but most people don't think that counts), and have
decided that I have the kind of aversion to doing so that RAW
addresses in his "Dissociation of Ideas I" exercise (whose point, for
those who might not have read about it, involves coming up with 20
counterexamples to any ideas that I take for granted to the point
of exhibiting knee-jerk behavior with respect to them).

I have done the exercise twice so far.  It took me two hours of
concerted effort to come up with 20 inventions we could do without,
and three days off and on to come up with 20 good things about getting
up early.  I expect that any idea ingrained enough to warrant doing
the exercise on would prove similarly challenging.  However, I
don't think that I could come up with 20 benefits to giving up control
of myself, no matter how long I could take. 

I associate drugs with lack of control, and I feel petrified at the
thought of lack of control.  It seems particularly stupid to me to
take drugs when around other people taking them, because if I did
something stupid like drinking Liquid Drano (TM) or breaking
furniture, people who would otherwise have the presence of mind to
stop me might not.

Discussion, please.

Thanks,
